# oracle: ReaxFF with fix qeq/reaxff (charges solved every step; qfile param.qeq from the LAMMPS RDX example, b332f28, GPL-2.0), RDX cell 105 atoms, 10 NVE steps
# measured: native and engine differ by one CG iteration from step 6 at tolerance 1e-6 (native tolerance-boundary noise, not reproduced); max rel error press 1.7e-5 (step 5), tight-tolerance twin w55reax_qeq_rdx_tight (tol 1e-12) agrees to 1e-9. So rel=1e-4 here.
# oracle-inputs: w55reax_rdx.data w55reax_rdx.control w55reax_param.qeq
# oracle-potentials: ffield.reax.rdx
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-4 abs=1e-6
units           real
atom_style      charge
boundary        p p p
read_data       w55reax_rdx.data
pair_style      reaxff w55reax_rdx.control
pair_coeff      * * ffield.reax.rdx H C O N
fix             2 all qeq/reax 1 0.0 10.0 1e-6 w55reax_param.qeq
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check no
timestep        0.25
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ebond evdwl ecoul ke etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             10
